{
  "category": "Elder Tree Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "It can control trees at will. It will trap people who harm the forest, so they can never leave.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using its roots as a nervous system, it controls the trees in the forest. It’s kind to the Pokémon that reside in its body.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "It can control trees at will. It will trap people who harm the forest, so they can never leave.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using its roots as a nervous system, it controls the trees in the forest. It’s kind to the Pokémon that reside in its body.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon is said to devour anyone daring to ravage the forest. To the creatures dwelling in the forest, it offers great kindness.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Through its roots, it exerts control over other trees. A deadly curse falls upon anyone cutting down trees in forests where Trevenant dwell.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It’s feared as a ghost of the forest. Lumberjacks bring along Fire types, which Trevenant hates, when they enter the forest.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon controls trees via roots stretching from its feet, and it will attack anyone that dares to ravage the forest.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "People fear it due to a belief that it devours any who try to cut down trees in its forest, but to the Pokémon it shares its woods with, it’s kind.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "Small roots that extend from the tips of this Pokémon’s feet can tie into the trees of the forest and give Trevenant control over them.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
